# Skill Output Structure

When a skill produces deliverables worth keeping (audits, plans, checklists, matrices, loop conditions, step summaries), write them under `.cursor/skill-outputs/` — never scatter skill artifacts in source trees, `.cursor/tools/`, or application code.

## Path layout

```text
.cursor/skill-outputs/
  {feature}/
    {layer}/
      {timestamp}_{skill-name}/
        {NN}_{step-slug}.md          # numbered step summaries (optional)
        {canonical-artifact}         # fixed-name deliverables (see catalog)
        {subfolder}/                 # grouped artifacts (e.g. loop/)
```

| Segment | Format | Example |
|---------|--------|---------|
| `feature` | kebab-case product area | `editor`, `export`, `onboarding`, `qa` |
| `layer` | kebab-case layer from [pixelanea-agent-tools.mdc](./pixelanea-agent-tools.mdc) | `canvas`, `domain`, `shell` |
| `timestamp` | `YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS` (UTC, sortable) | `20260731T054200` |
| `skill-name` | kebab-case; basename of the skill folder | `pixelanea-frontend-standards`, `loop-management` |
| `step` | `{NN}_{step-slug}.md` — zero-padded, 2+ digits | `01_audit-tool-context.md` |

## Artifact catalog

Use **fixed canonical names** for skill deliverables. Use **numbered step files** for multi-step investigation/plan/implement/review workflows.

| Artifact | Path (under run folder) | Producer | Purpose |
|----------|-------------------------|----------|---------|
| Step summary | `{NN}_{step-slug}.md` | skill-implementer, standards skills | Goal / Outcome / Files per step |
| Validation guide | `test.md` | test-writer agent | Executable post-delivery test guide |
| Unit test matrix | `test_matrix_unit.md` | test-matrix-unit | ID'd cases with live Status cells |
| Gherkin spec (optional) | `gherkin.md` | qa-e2e-gherkin | Matrix-derived E2E scenarios when not in changelog |
| QA run report | `qa_run_report.md` | qa-gherkin-run | Flagged scenario results beside gherkin source |
| Loop config | `loop/loop_config.json` | loop-management | Orchestrator paths, caps, next prompt |
| Loop stop check | `loop/check_condition.sh` | loop-management | Bash script; exit 0 = stop loop |
| Loop stop summary | `loop/stop_condition.md` | loop-management | One-sentence definition of exit 0 |
| Previous agent response | `loop/last_agent_response.md` | loop orchestrator | Overwritten each iteration |
| Loop iteration state | `loop/loop_iteration.json` | `loop_management.js` | Iteration counter; tool-managed |

**Loop rule:** All loop conditions, configs, checks, and response snapshots live under `loop/` inside the run folder — never in `.cursor/tools/`, repo root, or source trees.

**Changelog vs skill-outputs:** `gherkin.md` and `uxui_design_critique.md` may also live under `.cursor/changelog/` per their agents. Matrix and loop artifacts stay in `.cursor/skill-outputs/` only.

## Example runs

### Standards / implementer (numbered steps)

```text
.cursor/skill-outputs/
  editor/
    canvas/
      20260731T054200_pixelanea-frontend-standards/
        01_investigation.md
        02_plan.md
        03_refactor-input-routing.md
        04_code-review.md
        test.md
```

### Test matrix

```text
.cursor/skill-outputs/
  qa/
    paint/
      20260731T223100_test-matrix-unit/
        test_matrix_unit.md
        gherkin.md                    # optional sibling
```

### Loop management

```text
.cursor/skill-outputs/
  orchestration/
    test-matrix/
      20260731T224800_loop-management/
        loop/
          loop_config.json
          check_condition.sh
          stop_condition.md
          last_agent_response.md
          loop_iteration.json
        01_setup-loop.md              # optional step note
```

## Step file contents

Each `{NN}_{step-slug}.md` should be self-contained:

1. **Goal** — what this step set out to do (one sentence).
2. **Outcome** — decisions, findings, or changes produced.
3. **Files** — paths touched or reviewed (if any).

Keep steps atomic: one concern per file; add `02_`, `03_`, … for later steps in the same run.

## Subfolders

Use a subfolder when a run mixes **numbered steps** with **tool-driven or fixed-name bundles**:

| Subfolder | When |
|-----------|------|
| `loop/` | loop-management orchestration (required for loop skills) |
| Other | Only when a skill defines a named bundle; prefer flat fixed names otherwise |

All paths inside `loop_config.json` must be repo-relative and point under the same run folder's `loop/` directory.

## When to write

- **Do** persist outputs when the skill spans multiple steps or the user may revisit the work.
- **Do** create the full directory chain (including `loop/` when applicable) before the first file.
- **Do** keep tool-readable artifacts (JSON, shell checks) beside human markdown in the same run folder.
- **Don't** write here for trivial one-line answers or pure in-chat explanations.
- **Don't** duplicate application source code — link paths and summarize instead.
- **Don't** put one-off loop logic in `.cursor/tools/` — put checks in `loop/check_condition.sh`.
